The center of the reject-cluster anchors is ~5.0. The paper modestly exceeds these in rigor of evaluation and breadth of ablation, but falls short of the accept cluster due to the missing averaged-prototype ablation (which is the pivotal experiment for the main claim) and lack of statistical reporting. I place this at **5.0** — a borderline rejection.

**Originality**: Moderate. Applying CIVD/PD to TTA is new; the VD connection to nearest-neighbor classifiers is not.
**Importance**: Moderate. TTA is an active and practically important area; calibrated predictions are valuable.
