3. **Add a regret plot** (or equivalently, plot cumulative reward relative to the offline benchmark T·ν*) so experimental validation directly corresponds to the stated regret bounds.
4. **Provide baseline hyperparameter details in the main text** (at least a one-sentence summary of what values δb and Z were supplied to PGD Adaptive and SquareCBwK, and whether they were tuned or set to oracle values).
5. **Discuss lower bounds or hardness** for the no-strict-feasibility setting more substantively — even a brief argument about why T^{3/4} might be tight (or not) would strengthen Remark 2.

